*.synctex.gz

# Never carry publisher PDFs into this repository.
*.pdf
!figures/*.pdf
!supplementary-materials/*.pdf

# Release archives, written by scripts/make_release_archive.py. **This line is
# finding T-1 again, caught before it bit rather than after.** The archive is a
# zip *of the bundle*, written into the bundle; without this it enters the file
# set the fingerprint is taken over, so building a release would change the
# manifest, which would invalidate the archive that had just been built. The
# generator's own gate found it on its first run — it reported the archive as a
# file the manifest did not know about — which is the portability gate and the
# manifest check doing precisely what T-1 added them for.
dist/

# OS and editor metadata. Windows Explorer writes Thumbs.db into any folder of
# images --- figures/ --- and macOS writes .DS_Store into any folder opened in
# Finder. Neither is part of the bundle on any machine, and before finding T-1
# either could enter the release fingerprint just by someone looking at a
# directory. That is why these are listed rather than assumed absent.
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
*~
*.swp
*.swo
